<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vachutyan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vachutyans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vachutyans were an Armenian princely family of the 13th and 14th centuries, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the Zakarid rulers of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. They held lands in Aragatsotn, around the monasteries of Hovhannavank and Saghmosavank, which they rebuilt and endowed. Their founder Vache Vachutyan received his domains from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakarids">Zakarids</a> in the early 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vachutyan.jpg" alt="Vachutyan" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shaun Dunphy · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hovhannavank_-_gavit_(restoration).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
